  "asr_text": "It was a small twist. Behind a service that lets people ask AI to make phone calls, humans were actually making the calls. That kind of test was being carried out. The main player was Muse, Meta's AI assistant. Muse can call businesses and stores in the United States to book haircuts, check whether items are in stock, and get price estimates from businesses. If AI can take care of troublesome phone calls, it seems very useful. However, in some tests of its calling feature, trained human contract workers made the calls instead of AI. They handled the conversations all the way to the end. The issue was not that humans made the calls themselves. The issue was how to tell users who was speaking.",
